        {
          "title": "Automated Standardization of Legacy Biomedical Metadata Using an Ontology-Constrained LLM Agent",
          "title_zh": "使用本体约束的 LLM 智能体自动标准化遗留生物医学元数据",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2604.08552v5",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2604.08552",
          "summary": "ARMS is a tool-using LLM agent that retrieves CEDAR metadata templates and queries authoritative biomedical terminology services at runtime to standardize legacy metadata. On 839 records it raised precision from 0.56 to 0.93 and recall from 0.51 to 0.85 versus prompt engineering, with the largest gains on ontology-constrained fields.",
